      <bpmn:userTask id="W3807_Task4" name="Global Sourcing/Logistics-Finance track total-landed-cost (TLC) variance…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Global Sourcing/Logistics-Finance track total-landed-cost (TLC) variance: actual vs planned FOB, freight, duty, brokerage, financing, shrink per SKU/source/route (links to W3788), identify variance drivers, and feed corrective action
Responsible (R): Global Sourcing / Logistics Finance
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising / Finance
Duration: Monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3807_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3807_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3807_Task5" name="Global Sourcing/Finance measure realized import savings (negotiated FOB…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Global Sourcing/Finance measure realized import savings (negotiated FOB savings, consolidation savings, freight optimization, duty/PTA savings) vs target and confirm flow-through to margin/retail (links to VS-101/W3796), preventing &quot;negotiated but not realized&quot; leakage
Responsible (R): Global Sourcing / Finance / Merchandise Finance
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising / CFO
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3807_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3807_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3807_Task6" name="Global Sourcing/Merchandising link TLC to category margin and pricing decisions…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Global Sourcing/Merchandising link TLC to category margin and pricing decisions (links to VS-01.2/VS-101), ensuring import sourcing supports the 28–32% gross-margin and 6–8x turn targets
Responsible (R): Global Sourcing / Merchandising
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3807_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
